  "summary": "StreamReadConstraints.maxDocumentLength was not enforced for fixed-buffer and\nDataInput input. The document-length limit was added in 2.16.0 (f511bcd0, #1101),\non top of StreamReadConstraints, which was added in 2.15.0. At tag\njackson-core-2.14.0-rc2 there is no StreamReadConstraints class and no\nvalidateDocumentLength / maxDocumentLength anywhere under src/, so there is no\nlimit to bypass. Upstream lists the 2.x range as \u003e= 2.16.0, \u003c 2.18.7 and\n\u003e= 2.19.0, \u003c 2.21.2.\n",
